# patching-hosts host knob (#375). Grammar: skills/patching-hosts/references/knob.md
# (the vendored skill). The skill reads this file and never writes it. Times
# are UTC. A malformed line makes the host report-only until it is fixed.
# Held by tests/deploy/test_patching_knob.py: change a decision there first.

class production
posture scheduled

# --- when -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's window, weekly, Sun 22:00-24:00 Pacific (decided 2026-11-13,
# #375): the one Sunday-evening slot clear of every other cohort host's
# window and of this host's quiet ranges. A knob time is UTC and the weekday
# is the UTC day the range starts, so it is Monday here: Sun 22:00 PST is
# Mon 06:00Z. Fixed in UTC, it reads Sun 23:00-01:00 PDT from 2027-03-14;
# move it then if the slot is meant to hold in Pacific time. Every step's
# whole span, the bulk's including the reboot, must fit inside it.
cadence weekly
window Mon 06:00-08:00

# archiver-backup.timer: 03:17 UTC daily, RandomizedDelaySec=10min,
# AccuracySec=1min; the dump and upload take about a second. Outside the
# window: kept so that widening the window can't put a step on the backup.
quiet 03:15-03:45
# cannobserv-disk-gc.timer, the cohort disk GC (#440): 05:15 UTC daily,
# RandomizedDelaySec=30min, AccuracySec unset (1min). Its run takes minutes;
# the range keeps 14 of them past the last start (05:46). Its sensor, every
# 10 min, only reads; neither unit is in /etc/systemd/system, so the
# restarter scan doesn't read them.
quiet 05:15-06:00
# archiver-temporal-boundary.timer: 00:05 UTC daily, about a second. Its
# Persistent= catches up a run missed while down, never one a restart killed.
quiet 00:00-00:10

# --- the service ----------------------------------------------------------
# One process: the API, the dashboard, the bus consumers and the outbox
# publisher. Its restart is a full outage; the outbox catches the bus up.
service archiver.service

# The timer services running now: backup, bus-health, drift, pm-org-refresh,
# temporal-boundary, every one a Type=oneshot named archiver-*.service. The
# hourly two run on OnUnitActiveSec= and drift through the hour, so no quiet
# line can hold them: this gate catches them at each step. Reads unit state
# only, as exedev: never /etc/archiver/.env (root 0600, #339).
inflight systemctl list-units 'archiver-*.service' --state=activating,active,deactivating --no-legend --plain | grep -v '^archiver\.service' | wc -l

# Loopback: uvicorn binds 0.0.0.0:8000. /health is unauthenticated and
# DB-free; an authenticated GET on 8000 upserts AppUser on production.
health curl -sf -m5 http://127.0.0.1:8000/health | jq -e '.status == "ok"'

# After a Postgres restart: the read role (#348) is served, and the outbox
# publisher reached the database again, with nothing older than 2 minutes
# left unpublished. Proves little when nothing was written in the meantime.
recovery psql -d archiver -XAtc "select count(*) from information.changes_outbox where published_at is null and dead_lettered_at is null and created_at < now() - interval '2 minutes'" | grep -qx 0

# --- the data store -------------------------------------------------------
# The cluster holds archiver, archiver_dev and archiver_test. Only archiver
# is production data; the other two are excepted below rather than declared,
# because archiver-backup.service dumps archiver alone (--database archiver).
datastore postgres postgresql@16-main archiver
# The nightly dump to GCS (#233), create-only, checked in to co-status: the
# recovery point starts it and needs a fresh success instead of a second dump.
backup archiver-backup.service postgresql@16-main

# --- third-party origins --------------------------------------------------
# Each followed origin is scoped by a tracked pin file, installed under
# /etc/apt/preferences.d/ (deploy/apt-preferences.d/, deploy/README.md).
# NodeSource: nodejs, for SocratiCode's npx MCP server and the npm tooling.
origin deb.nodesource.com follow
# Tailscale carries the bus to broker and the co-status check-ins. Its
# postinst restarts tailscaled, a bus outage the outbox absorbs: its own
# step. Its own auto-update goes off on the node and for the tailnet in
# #375's host steps; the probe reads the node's at every run.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale-archive-keyring tailscale

# --- language dependencies -----------------------------------------------
# Every unit runs from /srv/archiver/live, a release built from this repo's
# uv.lock (#330), with no git remote for the probe to read.
owner /srv/archiver/live self

# --- callers --------------------------------------------------------------
# Replicator reads through archiver-client. Watcher makes no HTTP call either
# way: the edge is bus-only (#142). CannObserv/cli resolves with no token
# here; if it calls this host, it is a private caller, told by hand.
caller CannObserv/replicator

# --- exceptions -----------------------------------------------------------
exception database:archiver_test 2027-05-31 the suite's database (tests/conftest.py), its schema dropped every session; nothing in it to recover
exception database:archiver_dev 2027-05-31 the dev server's database (scripts/dev_server.sh), rebuilt on demand; nothing in it to recover
exception not-restarter:archiver-backup.service 2027-05-31 archiver_backup running pg_dump, pg_restore and the GCS upload (src.core.backup); starts nothing
exception not-restarter:archiver-bus-health.service 2027-05-31 a WARN-only outbox and stream probe (src.core.bus_health); starts nothing
exception not-restarter:archiver-drift.service 2027-05-31 asks GitHub whether live lags main and checks in (src.core.drift); starts nothing
exception not-restarter:archiver-pm-org-refresh.service 2027-05-31 one Power Map follower sweep (src.core.tools.refresh_orgs); starts nothing
exception not-restarter:archiver-temporal-boundary.service 2027-05-31 one temporal-profile evaluation (src.core.tools.temporal_boundary); starts nothing
# No image-owner line: this repo is public and the image repo is not
# (gregoryfoster/skills#350).
